1.2. Challenges in AR-HUD Crash Warning Icon Systems Design
AR-HUD icon systems aim to reduce vehicular collision incidents by promptly issuing potential risk notifications to drivers which can be categorized into two main types: screenfixed icons and world-relative icons [11]. Screen-fixed icons display information at fixed positions on the HUD interface, a method commonly employed in many current HUD systems [12]. Many driving studies exploring AR-HUD icon systems have utilized screenfixed display schemes, as evidenced in studies [13–19]. With advancements in tracking and spatial localization technologies, AR icons can now be associated with the real driving

