The study results reveal statistically significant effects of AR crash warning icon systems on total gaze time across different road conditions. For left-turn scenarios, no statistically significant differences were observed among the BD, BR, and BW groups. However, in straight-ahead and right-turn road conditions, the BW group demonstrated significantly different total gaze times compared to both the BD and BR groups, while no statistically significant difference was found between the BD and BR groups. These findings suggest that the BW type of AR warning icon exhibits more pronounced effectiveness in enhancing driver attention.
3.2. Number of Fixations
Further analysis reveals a significant interaction effect between AR crash warning icon systems and vehicle turning lanes on the number of fixation points within AOIs. Consequently, separate effect tests were conducted for the two within-subject factors (icon type and turning lane). The individual effect test for turning lanes involved comparing the differences in the number of fixation points among the three turning lanes under different types of AR crash warning icon systems. Table 5 presents the detailed results of the within-subject effects test, while Table 6 provides pairwise comparisons between different turning lanes.
The fixation points for drivers under three types of AR crash warning icon systems across different turning lanes are illustrated in Figure 7a. The impact of turning lane on fixation points is not statistically significant within the BD group. Conversely, within the BR group, this impact is significant. There is no significant difference between the left-turn and straight lanes. However, the disparity between left-turn and right-turn lanes is statistically significant (p = 0.001). Moreover, the difference between straight and right-turn lanes is not significant. Lastly, within the BW group, the influence of turning lane on fixation points is not statistically significant.

